ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE SPECIAL ACT ON DEVELOPMENT OF THE EAST, WEST, AND SOUTH COASTS AND INLAND AREAS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Special Act on Development of the East, West, and South Coasts and Inland Areas and matters necessary for its enforcement. <Amended on October 14, 2010>

Article 2 (Procedures for Preparing Comprehensive Plans)
(1) The relevant Metropolitan City Mayors, Special Self-Governing City Mayors, and Do Governors (hereinafter referred to as "Mayor/Do Governor") who intend to prepare a draft comprehensive plan for development of the East, West, or South Coastal Areas or inland areas (hereinafter referred to as "draft comprehensive plan") pursuant to Article 5 of the Special Act on Development of the East, West, and South Coasts and Inland Areas (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall jointly prepare the draft comprehensive plan, publicly announce its main contents in at least one daily newspaper whose principal circulation area is the Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, or Do under their jurisdiction (hereinafter referred to as "Si/Do") and in the official bulletin and on the website of the Si/Do, and send the draft comprehensive plan to the heads of the competent Sis/Guns/Gus (the head of a Gu means the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) so that it is available for public inspection for at least 14 days. <Amended on October 14, 2010; May 28, 2014>
(2) Any person who has an opinion on a draft comprehensive plan publicly announced under paragraph (1) may submit a written opinion to the relevant Special Self-Governing City Mayor or head of a Si/Gun/Gu during the inspection period. <Amended on May 28, 2014>
(3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall submit the written opinions submitted under paragraph (2), together with written comments on those opinions, to the Mayor/Do Governor.
(4) The Mayor/Do Governor shall consider whether to reflect the opinions submitted under paragraph (2) (applicable only to a Special Self-Governing City Mayor) and paragraph (3), and notify the persons who submitted them of the results within 60 days from the end of the inspection period. <Amended on May 28, 2014>
(5) When holding a public hearing pursuant to Article 5 (2) of the Act, the Mayor/Do Governor shall publicly announce each of the following at least once, no later than 14 days before the scheduled hearing date, in at least one daily newspaper whose principal circulation area is the Si/Do under his or her jurisdiction and in the official bulletin and on the website of the Si/Do:
1. The purpose of the public hearing;
2. The scheduled date, time, and place of the public hearing;
3. An outline of the draft comprehensive plan to be prepared.

Article 3 (Criteria for Designation and Scope of East, West, and South Coastal Areas and Inland Areas)
(1) The criteria for designation of the East, West, and South Coastal Areas (hereinafter referred to as "coastal areas") under Article 5 (3) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on October 14, 2010; June 4, 2024; December 24, 2024; June 23, 2026>
1. East Coastal Area: Basic local governments (meaning local governments under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Local Autonomy Act; hereinafter the same shall apply) within the jurisdictions of Ulsan Metropolitan City, Gangwon Special Self-Governing Province, and Gyeongsangbuk-do that adjoin the coastline;
2. West Coastal Area: Basic local governments within the jurisdictions of Incheon Metropolitan City, Gyeonggi-do, Chungcheongnam-do, and Jeonbuk Special Self-Governing Province that adjoin the coastline;
3. South Coastal Area: Basic local governments within the jurisdictions of Busan Metropolitan City, Jeonnam-Gwangju Integrated Special City, and Gyeongsangnam-do that adjoin the coastline.
(2) The criteria for designation of inland areas under Article 5 (3) of the Act shall be as follows: <Newly Inserted on May 28, 2014; Amended on June 4, 2024; December 24, 2024; June 23, 2026>
1. Baekdudaegan Area: Basic local governments in inland regions within the jurisdictions of Gangwon Special Self-Governing Province, Chungcheongbuk-do, Jeonbuk Special Self-Governing Province, Jeonnam-Gwangju Integrated Special City, Gyeongsangbuk-do, and Gyeongsangnam-do that are located in or adjacent to the Baekdudaegan under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Act on the Protection of the Baekdudaegan;
2. Inland Advanced Industry Area: Basic local governments in inland regions within the jurisdictions of Daejeon Metropolitan City, Sejong Special Self-Governing City, Gangwon Special Self-Governing Province, Chungcheongbuk-do, Chungcheongnam-do, and Jeonbuk Special Self-Governing Province that are located west of the Baekdudaegan Area under subparagraph 1;
3. Daegu-Gwangju Cooperation Area: Basic local governments in inland regions within the jurisdictions of Daegu Metropolitan City, Jeonnam-Gwangju Integrated Special City (limited to Dong-gu, Seo-gu, Nam-gu, Buk-gu, and Gwangsan-gu), and the nearby areas of Jeonnam-Gwangju Integrated Special City and Gyeongsangbuk-do.
(3) The specific scope of coastal areas and inland areas shall be as prescribed in attached Table 1. <Amended on October 14, 2010; May 28, 2014; August 9, 2017>

Article 4 (Minor Changes to Comprehensive Plans)
"Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 6 (1) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on October 14, 2010; July 30, 2019>
1. Where the area of a coastal area or inland area development project (hereinafter referred to as "development project") reflected in a comprehensive plan for coastal areas or inland areas (hereinafter referred to as "comprehensive plan") is changed within 10 percent;
2. Where the implementation period of a development project reflected in a comprehensive plan is shortened, or extended by no more than three years;
3. Where, after major infrastructure for which a project plan has been finalized under another Act is reflected in a comprehensive plan, the relevant project plan is changed or abolished and such change or abolition is reflected therein;
4. Where the details of a development project are changed to an extent that does not alter its basic direction.

Article 5 (Public Notification of Comprehensive Plans)
(1) When a comprehensive plan is determined or changed pursuant to Article 6 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publicly notify its main contents in the Official Gazette and send copies of the relevant documents, drawings, etc. to the heads of the relevant administrative agencies and local governments. <Amended on March 23, 2013>
(2) A Special Self-Governing City Mayor or head of a Si/Gun/Gu who receives copies of the relevant documents, drawings, etc. pursuant to paragraph (1) shall make them available for public inspection for at least 14 days. <Amended on May 28, 2014>

Article 6 (Minor Changes to Designation of Development Zones)
"Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of the portion other than the subparagraphs of Article 7 (1) of the Act and in the proviso to paragraph (4) of that Article means any of the following cases: <Amended on December 15, 2009; October 14, 2010>
1. Where the area of a coastal area or inland area development zone (hereinafter referred to as "development zone") is reduced;
2. Where the area of a development zone is expanded within 10 percent: Provided, That if an area into which the development zone is to be expanded includes any of the following zones, prior consultation shall be held with the head of the relevant central administrative agency:
(a) An area determined and publicly notified as an area subject to land reclamation under Article 13 (4) of the Rural Community Improvement Act;
(b) A military base and military installation protection zone under Article 2, subparagraph 6 of the Protection of Military Bases and Installations Act.

Article 7 (Requirements for Designation of Development Zones)
"Other requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7 (1) 5 of the Act means the following requirements:
1. The development zone shall have a substantial effect on stimulating the regional economy, including increasing employment;
2. It shall have a substantial effect on regional development through connections with development projects under other statutes that are underway or planned in nearby areas.

Article 8 (Areas in Which Development Plans Are Prepared after Designation of Development Zones)
"Areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 7 (2) of the Act means areas, other than urban areas under Article 6, subparagraph 1 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act, that need development plans to be established in stages for systematic development and that are designated and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 9 (Hearing Opinions on Designation of and Changes to Development Zones)
(1) A Mayor/Do Governor who intends to hear opinions on a request for designation of or a change to a development zone pursuant to the main clause of Article 7 (4) of the Act shall send copies of the relevant documents to the heads of the competent Sis/Guns/Gus.
(2) A Special Self-Governing City Mayor or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who receives the relevant documents pursuant to paragraph (1) shall, without delay, publicly announce the name, location, area, etc. of the development zone proposed for designation or change in the official bulletin and on the website of the competent Si/Gun/Gu (a Gu means an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply), and make the relevant documents available for public inspection for at least 14 days. <Amended on May 28, 2014>
(3) Any person who has an opinion on designation of a development zone may submit a written opinion to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor or head of the Si/Gun/Gu during the inspection period under paragraph (2). <Amended on May 28, 2014>
(4) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall submit to the Mayor/Do Governor his or her written opinion on designation of the development zone, the written opinions submitted under paragraph (3), and written comments on those opinions.
(5) The Mayor/Do Governor shall consider whether to reflect the opinions submitted under paragraph (3) (applicable only to a Special Self-Governing City Mayor) and paragraph (4), and notify the persons who submitted them of the results within 60 days from the end of the inspection period. <Amended on May 28, 2014>

Article 10 (Public Notification of Designation of and Changes to Development Zones)
When designating or changing a development zone pursuant to Article 7 (5) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publicly notify the following matters in the Official Gazette and notify the heads of the relevant administrative agencies and local governments thereof: <Amended on March 23, 2013>
1. The name of the development zone;
2. The location and area of the development zone;
3. The purpose of designation of or change to the development zone and the basic direction of development;
4. A map showing the location of the development zone;
5. Topographical drawings under Article 8 (3) of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use, or drawings indicating areas, districts, etc. on cadastral maps, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "topographical drawings, etc.").

Article 11 (Size of Development Zones)
The size of an area that may be designated as a development zone pursuant to Article 7 (7) of the Act shall be at least 30,000 square meters: Provided, That where the area to be designated is outside an urban area under Article 6, subparagraph 1 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act and the plan includes construction of apartments or row houses among the multi-family housing under subparagraph 2 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act, its size shall be at least 300,000 square meters. <Amended on June 11, 2013>

Article 12 (Documents Required for Requests for Designation of Development Zones)
(1) When a Mayor/Do Governor requests the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to designate or change a development zone pursuant to Article 7 of the Act, he or she shall submit the following materials to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport: <Amended on April 10, 2012; March 23, 2013>
1. The results of hearing opinions under Article 7 (4) of the Act;
2. Relevant documents and drawings necessary to determine or change an urban/Gun management plan under Article 30 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (hereinafter referred to as "urban/Gun management plan");
3. Information on urban/Gun planning facilities determined by an urban/Gun management plan or installed pursuant to Article 43 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act in areas surrounding the development zone;
4. Relevant documents and drawings necessary for determination of a district-unit planning zone under Article 50 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act for areas surrounding the development zone (hereinafter referred to as "determination of a district-unit plan");
5. A report on the results of the basic survey under Article 13 of the Act;
6. Topographical drawings, etc.;
7. A location map at a scale of at least 1:25,000 indicating the location of the development zone;
8. A cadastral map or forest land map indicating the boundaries of the development zone;
9. Survey materials on the current status of land and forest land to be incorporated;
10. Photographs showing current conditions.
(2) "Materials prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 7 (8) of the Act means the materials under Article 71 (1) 1 through 3, 5, and 6 of the Building Act.

Article 13 (Buildings Subject to Deliberation in Development Zones and Matters for Deliberation)
(1) "Buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7 (9) of the Act means the following buildings: <Amended on October 14, 2010; December 29, 2017>
1. Buildings subject to a building permit under Article 11 of the Building Act in a landscape district under Article 37 (1) 1 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
2. Buildings under the subparagraphs of Article 70 of the Building Act.
(2) When a building committee established by a Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deliberates on a building pursuant to Article 7 (9) of the Act, its deliberation shall include the following matters: <Newly Inserted on October 14, 2010; Amended on December 29, 2017>
1. Matters concerning restrictions on construction in landscape districts under Article 72 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
2. Matters concerning special exceptions to application of relevant statutes under Article 73 of the Building Act;
3. Matters concerning architectural design under Article 3, subparagraph 4 of the Framework Act on Building.

Article 14 (Ratio of Land Purchase in Relation to Revocation of Designation of Development Zones)
"Ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9 (1) 2 of the Act means 30/100 of the area of land subject to purchase within the relevant development zone. In such cases, when calculating the ratio of land purchase, land owned since 2 years before the date of public notice of designation of the development zone by an implementer of a development project designated pursuant to Article 11 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "project implementer") or by a person who has invested in a project implementer shall be excluded.

Article 15 (Public Notice of Revocation of Designation of Development Zones)
Upon revoking the designation of a development zone pursuant to Article 9 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publicly notify the following matters in the Official Gazette: <Amended 2013.3.23>
1. The name of the development zone;
2. The location and area of the development zone;
3. The grounds for revocation of designation of the development zone;
4. Matters concerning the reversion or abolition of use areas, use zones, and district-unit planning zones under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
5. Topographical drawings, etc.

Article 16 (Restrictions on Acts, etc.)
(1) Acts for which permission must be obtained from the competent Special Self-Governing City Mayor or head of a Si/Gun/Gu within a development zone pursuant to Article 10 (1) of the Act means any of the following acts: <Amended 2014.5.28, 2021.1.5>
1. Construction of buildings, etc.: Construction, major repair, or change of use of buildings (including temporary buildings) under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Building Act;
2. Installation of structures: Installation of artificial facilities (excluding buildings under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Building Act);
3. Alteration of the form and quality of land: Acts of altering the shape of land through cutting (cutting away land), filling (piling up soil), leveling (making land level), paving, or similar methods, excavation of land, or reclamation of public waters;
4. Extraction of earth and stones: Acts of extracting earth and stones, such as soil, sand, gravel, and rocks (excluding cases for the purpose of altering the form and quality of land under subparagraph 3);
5. Subdivision of land;
6. Acts of piling up objects: Acts of piling up objects that are not easily movable for at least 1 month;
7. Acts of cutting or planting bamboo and trees.
(2) "Other acts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (2) 2 of the Act means any of the following acts that are not subject to permission for development activities under Article 56 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act: <Amended 2013.3.23>
1. Alteration of the form and quality of land for cultivation;
2. Temporary planting of ornamental bamboo and trees (excluding temporary planting of trees on cultivated land);
3. Installation of simple structures prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport that are directly used for the production of agricultural, forestry, and fishery products.
(3) Pursuant to Article 10 (3) of the Act, a person who has not completed construction work or a project shall report the progress of the relevant construction work, etc. to the competent Special Self-Governing City Mayor or head of a Si/Gun/Gu within 30 days from the date of public notice of designation of the development zone, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended 2013.3.23, 2014.5.28>
(4) When granting permission for an act specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) pursuant to Article 10 (1) of the Act, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor or head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall hear the opinion of the project implementer in advance if a project implementer has already been designated. <Amended 2014.5.28>

Article 17 (Documents for Application for Designation as Project Implementer, etc.)
(1) A person who intends to be designated as a project implementer pursuant to Article 11 (1) of the Act shall submit to the designating authority an application for designation as a project implementer for development of coastal areas or inland areas, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, together with the following documents and drawings: Provided, That this shall not apply where the State or a Si/Do implements the project. <Amended 2010.10.14, 2013.3.23>
1. A project plan;
2. A financing plan (including documents that enable verification of financial soundness and the stability of equity capital where a person falling under Article 11 (1) 5 of the Act applies);
3. A location map at a scale of 1:25,000 or 1:50,000.
(2) Matters necessary for the designation of project implementers, etc., other than those prescribed in paragraph (1), shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended 2013.3.23>

Article 18 (Minor Changes to Development Plans)
"Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 12 (1) of the Act means the following cases: <Amended 2019.7.30>
1. Where project costs are increased or decreased within a range of 10/100;
2. Where the area for installation of equipment and facilities is increased or decreased within a range of 10/100;
3. Where the implementation period of a development project is shortened or extended by up to 3 years;
4. Where the address of the project implementer is changed;
5. Where the representative of a project implementer that is a corporation is changed.

Article 19 (Natural Parks and Types and Sizes of Park Facilities)
(1) "Natural parks prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 12 (2) of the Act means the following natural parks designated pursuant to Article 4 of the Natural Parks Act:
1. Hallyeohaesang National Park;
2. Dadohaehaesang National Park.
(2) "Types and sizes of park facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 12 (2) of the Act means the following: <Amended 2010.10.14>
1. Excursion boat docks: A site area of not more than 15,000 square meters;
2. Trails: A width of not more than 3 meters (not more than 6 meters for sections through which vehicles pass);
3. Observation decks: A site area of not more than 3,000 square meters (not more than 400 square meters where all or part of the observation deck is installed in a park nature conservation district under Article 18 (1) 1 of the Natural Parks Act).

Article 20 (Approval of Development Plans, etc.)
(1) "Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12 (2) 14 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Drawings prepared by indicating the development plan on a topographical map or cadastral map at a scale of 1:5,000 or larger;
2. A plan for integrated energy supply;
3. Matters concerning the opinion of the competent head of a Si/Gun/Gu and whether it has been reflected.
(2) When publicly notifying a development plan pursuant to Article 12 (3) of the Act, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall include the following matters: <Amended 2013.3.23>
1. The name of the development plan;
2. The name and address of the project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. The implementation period of the development project;
4. A land use plan;
5. The location and area of the land to be developed;
6. A plan for installation of major infrastructure, such as roads, water supply systems, and sewerage systems;
7. A financing plan and annual investment plans;
8. A detailed list of land, etc. where it is intended to expropriate or use such land, etc. pursuant to Article 16 (1) of the Act.

Article 21 Deleted <2010.10.14>

Article 22 (Preparation of Basic Survey Plans, etc.)
(1) When conducting a basic survey pursuant to Article 13 (1) of the Act, a Mayor/Do Governor or project implementer shall prepare a basic survey plan that includes the purpose, target area, period, methods, and contents of the survey, etc.
(2) When conducting a basic survey, a Mayor/Do Governor or project implementer may have any of the following persons conduct the basic survey on his or her behalf: <Amended 2011.1.17>
1. A government-funded research institution under Article 8 (1) of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes;
2. A public institution under Article 4 (1) of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
3. A local research institute under Article 4 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Local Government-Funded Research Institutes (hereinafter referred to as a "local research institute");
4. A research institution related to regional development attached to a school specified in the subparagraphs of Article 2 of the Higher Education Act;
5. An engineering business operator that has filed a report pursuant to Article 21 of the Engineering Industry Promotion Act.

Article 23 (Scope of Basic Surveys, etc.)
(1) "Other matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13 (2) of the Act means the following:
1. The current status and trends of population changes;
2. The current status of land use;
3. The current status and development trends of each industry;
4. The current status of major infrastructure, such as roads, water supply systems, and sewerage systems;
5. The current status of tourism resources, types of tourism, and tourism facilities;
6. The state of conservation and actual conditions of pollution of the natural environment;
7. Relationships with higher-level plans and other plans for neighboring areas;
8. Other matters deemed necessary by the Mayor/Do Governor.
(2) When conducting a basic survey under Article 13 of the Act, data from surveys or measurements conducted pursuant to other statutes or regulations may be utilized if such data are available on the matters to be surveyed.

Article 24 (Approval of Implementation Plans, etc.)
(1) "Other documents or drawings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 14 (1) 6 of the Act means the following documents or drawings: <Amended 2012.4.10, 2012.7.20, 2024.5.7>
1. A compensation plan (including relocation measures);
2. A plan for the vesting and replacement of public facilities and land, etc.;
3. Relevant documents and drawings necessary for the determination of or amendment to an urban/Gun management plan (limited to cases where an urban/Gun management plan is determined or amended);
4. Relevant documents and drawings necessary for the determination of a district-unit plan (limited to cases where a district-unit plan is formulated);
5. Documents concerning a plan for division of construction sections (limited to cases where there is a division plan);
6. An environmental impact assessment report under Article 27 of the Environmental Impact Assessment Act (limited to projects subject to environmental impact assessment);
7. Documents concerning measures for the conservation of national heritage;
8. Documents necessary for consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies pursuant to Article 15 (2) of the Act;
9. A detailed list of land, etc. where it is intended to expropriate or use such land, etc. pursuant to Article 16 (1) of the Act.
(2) Public notice of an implementation plan under Article 14 (3) of the Act shall include the following matters:
1. The name of the project;
2. The name and address of the project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. An outline of the project;
4. A compensation plan (including relocation measures);
5. A plan for the vesting and replacement of public facilities and land, etc.;
6. Matters concerning the determination of a district-unit plan (limited to cases where a district-unit plan is formulated);
7. A detailed list of land, etc. where it is intended to expropriate or use such land, etc. pursuant to Article 16 (1) of the Act.
(3) "Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 14 (4) of the Act means the following cases: <Amended 2016.12.30>
1. Where project costs are increased or decreased within a range of 10/100;
2. Where the area for installation of equipment and facilities is increased or decreased within a range of 10/100;
3. Where the address of the project implementer is changed;
4. Where the representative of a project implementer that is a corporation is changed;
5. Where an area is changed to correct an error or omission or in accordance with survey results.

Article 25 (Permission for Persons Other Than Park Management Authorities to Implement Park Projects)
"Natural parks prescribed by Presidential Decree and facilities falling within the types and sizes of park facilities, such as excursion boat docks and trails, prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 15 (1) 22 of the Act means the natural parks and facilities falling within the types and sizes of park facilities under Article 19.

Article 26 (Entrustment of Duties Concerning Acquisition of Land, etc.)
(1) If a project implementer intends to entrust duties concerning the acquisition of land, objects, or rights and duties concerning compensation pursuant to Article 16 (4) of the Act, the project implementer shall consult with the person to be entrusted concerning the details, terms, etc. of the entrustment.
(2) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 16 (4) of the Act means institutions specified in the subparagraphs of Article 81 (1) of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works.

Article 27 (Completion Inspections, etc.)
(1) To undergo a completion inspection pursuant to Article 20 (1) of the Act, a project implementer (excluding the State and Sis/Dos) shall submit to the Mayor/Do Governor a construction completion report, together with the documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended 2013.3.23>
(2) When publicly announcing the completion of construction pursuant to Article 20 (3) of the Act, a Mayor/Do Governor shall publicly notify the following matters in the official gazette and on the website of the Si/Do under his or her jurisdiction:
1. The name of the project;
2. The project implementer;
3. The location of the project site;
4. The area of the project site and the area by use;
5. The date of completion;
6. Matters concerning the disposition of major facilities.

Article 28 (Criteria for Designation of Marine Tourism Promotion Districts)
"Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20-2 (5) 3 of the Act means the following criteria: <Amended on June 22, 2021>
1. The total area of the marine tourism promotion district shall be at least 100,000 square meters;
2. The marine tourism promotion district shall be an area falling under any of the following items:
(a) An area that includes land within 1,000 meters from the land boundary facing the sea as recorded in cadastral records;
(b) An area that includes the area under item (a) and nearby island areas [meaning island areas under Article 2 (1) of the Island Development Promotion Act; hereinafter the same shall apply];
(c) An area where the entire marine tourism promotion district consists of island areas;
3. The amount of private investment shall be at least 20 billion won;
4. Measures to minimize seawater pollution in the relevant area shall be prepared.

Article 29 (Special Cases concerning the Application of Relevant Acts in Marine Tourism Promotion Districts)
(1) Facilities that may be installed in the areas under Article 20-3 (1) 1 and 3 of the Act pursuant to the main clause of the introductory portion of that paragraph shall be as specified in attached Table 2.
(2) Under Article 20-3 (2) of the Act, the maximum building-to-land ratio in the areas under paragraph (1) 1 of that Article shall be 40 percent, and the maximum floor area ratio shall be 100 percent.

Article 30 (Composition of Joint Councils for Development of the East, West, and South Coastal Areas or Inland Areas)
(1) A Joint Council for Development of the East, West, and South Coastal Areas or Inland Areas under Article 22 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Council") shall be established for each coastal area and inland area and shall consist of not more than 24 members, including co-chairpersons. <Amended on October 14, 2010>
(2) The co-chairpersons of the Council for each coastal area and inland area (hereinafter referred to as the "co-chairpersons") shall be the relevant Mayors/Do Governors, and the members of the Council shall be the following persons: <Amended on October 14, 2010>
1. The chairpersons of the councils of the relevant Si/Do;
2. The heads of the local research institutes of the relevant Si/Do;
3. Persons commissioned by the co-chairpersons for each relevant Si/Do from among persons with extensive knowledge and experience in fields related to the development of coastal areas and inland areas, such as national land planning, tourism, logistics, science and technology, finance, and the environment.
(3) The term of office of members commissioned by a Mayor/Do Governor shall be three years, and they may be reappointed.

Article 31 (Operation of Councils)
(1) Meetings of the Council shall be held through consultation among the co-chairpersons, and the Mayor/Do Governor of the place where the meeting is held shall preside over the meeting.
(2) Meetings of the Council shall be convened with a majority of the members in office present, and resolutions shall be adopted with the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(3) Matters necessary for the operation of the Council, other than those provided for in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be prescribed by the co-chairpersons through consultation following a resolution of the Council.

Article 32 (Planning Group for Development of the East, West, and South Coasts and Inland Areas)
(1) The head of the Planning Group for Development of the East, West, and South Coasts and Inland Areas under Article 23 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Planning Group") shall be the First Vice Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and the deputy head shall be a person designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among public officials in general service who are members of the Senior Civil Service of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on October 14, 2010; March 23, 2013>
(2) Under the orders of the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, the head of the Planning Group shall exercise overall control over the affairs of the Planning Group and direct and supervise its members. <Amended on March 23, 2013>
(3) Where necessary for the performance of the duties of the Planning Group, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may request the secondment of public officials of relevant administrative agencies, officers and employees of relevant institutions and organizations, etc. <Amended on March 23, 2013>
(4) Matters necessary for the composition and operation of the Planning Group, other than those provided for in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be prescribed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 33 (Designation of Investment Promotion Districts, etc.)
(1) "Investment that meets the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 25 (1) of the Act means investment for the new installation of facilities to engage in businesses falling under the following subparagraphs, where the total project costs of the project to be implemented in an area intended to be designated as a coastal area or inland area investment promotion district (hereinafter referred to as an "investment promotion district") are at least five million United States dollars: <Amended on November 2, 2009; October 14, 2010; June 15, 2015; December 8, 2020; August 26, 2025>
1. Tourist hotel business, floating tourist hotel business, Korean traditional hotel business, specialized resort business, comprehensive resort business, tourist cruise ship business, tourist performance venue business, international conference facility business, and comprehensive theme park business under Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Tourism Promotion Act: Provided, That golf course business under Article 10 (1) 1 of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act shall be excluded from specialized resort business and comprehensive resort business;
2. Business of manufacturing or operating water leisure equipment under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Water-Related Leisure Activities Safety Act;
3. Cultural industries under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Framework Act on the Promotion of Cultural Industries;
4. Business of operating welfare facilities for older persons under Article 31 of the Welfare of Senior Citizens Act;
5. Business of operating youth training facilities under Article 10, subparagraph 1 of the Youth Activity Promotion Act;
6. Tramway business under Article 2, subparagraph 7 of the Tramway Transportation Act;
7. Projects for the use and diffusion, etc. of new energy and renewable energy under Article 2, subparagraphs 1 and 2 of the Act on the Promotion of the Development, Use and Diffusion of New and Renewable Energy;
8. Robot Land development projects under Article 31 of the Intelligent Robots Development and Distribution Promotion Act;
9. Aerospace industries under Article 4 of the Aerospace Industry Development Promotion Act;
10. Research and development projects for nanotechnology under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Nanotechnology Development Promotion Act;
11. Software business under Article 2, subparagraph 3 of the Software Promotion Act;
12. Business using advanced technologies under Article 5 of the Industrial Development Act (limited to the fields of electronics, electricity, information, new materials, and biotechnology);
13. Logistics facilities, logistics terminals, logistics complex facilities, support facilities, and logistics complex development projects under Article 2 of the Act on the Development and Operation of Logistics Facilities.
(2) Where a Mayor/Do Governor intends to designate an investment promotion district under Article 25 (1) of the Act, the Mayor/Do Governor shall formulate a plan for designation of the investment promotion district (hereinafter referred to as a "designation plan") that includes the following matters, consult with relevant administrative agencies, and then undergo deliberation by the National Land Policy Committee under Article 26 (1) of the Framework Act on the National Land (hereinafter referred to as the "National Land Policy Committee"): <Amended on May 30, 2012; July 20, 2012>
1. The name, location, and area of the investment promotion district;
2. The investor's personal name, trade name or corporate name, and nationality;
3. The method of development or management of the investment promotion district;
4. Investment particulars, the scale of employment, and details of the business;
5. The feasibility of implementing the investment sought to be attracted;
6. Costs and expected effects of designation of the investment promotion district;
7. A financing plan;
8. A plan for support for major facilities in the investment promotion district;
9. A land use plan and a plan for major infrastructure;
10. Materials related to a strategic environmental impact assessment or environmental impact assessment;
11. Other matters prescribed by the National Land Policy Committee.
(3) Where a Mayor/Do Governor intends to amend a designation plan, the Mayor/Do Governor shall consult with relevant administrative agencies and then undergo deliberation by the National Land Policy Committee: Provided, That this shall not apply to a minor amendment falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on May 30, 2012>
1. A change in the name of the development project;
2. A change in the investor's personal name, trade name, or corporate name;
3. A change in the implementation period of the development project;
4. A change within 10 percent of the area originally planned;
5. A change within 10 percent of the original investment amount;
6. A change within 10 percent of the original scale of employment;
7. A change in the land use plan or the plan for installation of major infrastructure due to topographical or geological conditions.
(4) When formulating or amending a designation plan (excluding a minor amendment under the proviso to paragraph (3)), a Mayor/Do Governor shall hear the opinions of the relevant head of a Si/Gun/Gu, residents, and relevant experts. In such cases, Article 9 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures for hearing opinions, etc.
(5) The National Land Policy Committee shall deliberate on whether to designate an investment promotion district based on the designation plan, comprehensively considering the feasibility of implementing the investment sought to be attracted, efficient land use, and impacts on the regional economy, such as increased employment. <Amended on May 30, 2012>
(6) Details necessary for the designation of investment promotion districts, etc. under paragraphs (1) through (5) shall be prescribed by the National Land Policy Committee. <Amended on May 30, 2012>

Article 34 (Revocation of Designation of Investment Promotion Districts)
(1) Where investment in an investment promotion district no longer meets the criteria for designation of an investment promotion district under Article 33 (1), a Mayor/Do Governor shall set a period not exceeding six months and order the investor to meet those criteria: Provided, That where an unavoidable reason is recognized, the Mayor/Do Governor may extend the period once by up to the length of the original compliance period.
(2) Where the investor fails to meet the designation criteria within the compliance period under paragraph (1), the Mayor/Do Governor shall request deliberation by the National Land Policy Committee on revocation of designation of the investment promotion district within 30 days after the compliance period expires. <Amended on May 30, 2012>
(3) Where a Mayor/Do Governor revokes the designation of an investment promotion district, the Mayor/Do Governor shall publicly notify that fact in the official gazette and on the website of the relevant Si/Do.
(4) Details necessary for revocation of designation of investment promotion districts under paragraphs (1) through (3) shall be prescribed by the National Land Policy Committee. <Amended on May 30, 2012>

Article 35 (Use of Marine Tourism Resources)
"Marine tourism resources prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 28 (2) 3 of the Act means any of the following: <Amended on October 14, 2010; June 22, 2021>
1. Tourism resources of islands under Article 2 (1) of the Island Development Promotion Act and port areas under Article 2, subparagraph 4 of the Harbor Act;
2. Tourism resources related to water leisure activities under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Water-Related Leisure Activities Safety Act;
3. Tourism resources of marina port areas under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Act on the Development, Management, etc. of Marina Ports.

Article 35-2 (Use of Closed School Property)
(1) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29-2 (1) 1 of the Act means youth training facilities under Article 10, subparagraph 1 of the Youth Activity Promotion Act.
(2) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29-2 (1) 2 of the Act means cultural facilities under Article 2 (1) 3 of the Culture and Arts Promotion Act.

Article 35-3 (Application Mutatis Mutandis to Projects Outside Development Zones)
(1) "Projects prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30-2 of the Act means the following projects: <Amended on March 23, 2013; July 30, 2019>
1. Projects to install roads, railways, waterworks, electricity and gas facilities, water supply facilities, sewage treatment facilities, and facilities related to waste treatment;
2. River improvement projects;
3. Other projects similar to those under subparagraphs 1 and 2 that the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems necessary to achieve the purposes of a development project.
(2) Deleted. <July 30, 2019>

Article 36 (Provision of National Treasury Subsidies)
(1) Projects for which increased subsidies may be provided under Article 31 (1) of the Act shall be determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in consultation with the Minister of Planning and Budget from among projects eligible for subsidies under Article 4 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Subsidy Management Act. <Amended on October 26, 2011; March 23, 2013; December 30, 2025>
(2) The increase in the subsidy rate for projects determined under paragraph (1) shall be determined, within a range of 20 percent, by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in consultation with the Minister of Planning and Budget. <Amended on March 23, 2013; December 30, 2025>

